    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFall back to torch.cuda and safe defaults in RocmPlatform.get_device_name, get_device_uuid, and is_fully_connected when amdsmi_init fails (such as on WSL2 where /dev/dxg is exposed instead of /dev/kfd).\n\nFixes #64664\n\n## Claims\n\n- Prevents RocmPlatform.get_device_name, get_device_uuid, and is_fully_connected from crashing with AmdSmiLibraryException when ROCm platform detection succeeds via the WSL PyTorch fallback (#38434) but AMDSMI cannot initialize.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npytest tests/test_zen_cpu_platform_detection.py -k test_rocm_platform_falls_back_when_amdsmi_fails -v\n```\n\n## Details\n\nWhile #38434 added a WSL PyTorch/HIP fallback to rocm_platform_plugin() when amdsmi_init() fails, and _get_gcn_arch() and RocmPlatform.get_device_total_memory() already catch AMDSMI exceptions and fall back to torch.cuda, RocmPlatform.get_device_name(), get_device_uuid(), and is_fully_connected() were decorated directly with @with_amdsmi_context. Wrapping the AMDSMI queries in helper functions and falling back to torch.cuda.get_device_name(device_id), \"rocm:{device_id}\", and False allows ROCm startup to proceed in WSL2 environments where AMDSMI is unavailable.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's /pr-checklist skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
